{
  "_comment": "Central button-to-runtime manifest for the AOS Command Center. 'script' and 'cwd' are relative to AOS/ (resolved via utils/paths.py's aos_path()); every button invokes 'script' as its own subprocess run from 'cwd', exactly mirroring AOS/orchestrator/orchestrator.py's own run_attempt() — the dashboard never imports a runtime module in-process. 'outputs' are the well-known files/dirs the page reads afterward for display, purely by existence/content, never by re-deriving business logic. This file documents the answer to the README's required 'how every button maps to the existing AOS runtime' section.",
  "orchestrator": {
    "label": "Run Full AOS",
    "script": "orchestrator/orchestrator.py",
    "cwd": "orchestrator",
    "timeoutSeconds": 900,
    "statusFile": "output/orchestrator/status.json",
    "logsDir": "output/orchestrator/logs",
    "reportsDir": "output/orchestrator/reports"
  },
